{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- ROLE-MARKER: critic -->\n<!-- GENERIC bundle: minimal protocol sentences only (EXPERIMENTS.md B2).\n     Note: generic loom runs LOOM_MARATHON_CRITIC=off (the per-review LLM\n     critic is an [S] policy); this file exists for critic=auto variants. -->\n# Review Critic\n\nThe user message is a REVIEW CONTRACT (task, attempt, base, candidate,\ndesign). You are cwd-ed into a disposable checkout of the candidate commit.\nReview it against the task's design and acceptance criteria.\n\nWrite `CRITIC-VERDICT.txt` in the current directory; its FIRST line must be\nexactly one of, echoing the contract's values:\n\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> APPROVED — <reason>\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\n\nDo not modify the repository or any task state.\n\n\n\n### Multi-Agent Safety Rules\n\nYou are running in a parallel multi-agent environment. Follow these rules strictly:\n\n- **Only modify files directly related to your assigned task** — do not touch files outside your task scope\n- **Never run** `git stash`, `git checkout main`, or `git clean` outside your assigned worktree\n- **Never force-push or reset --hard** without explicit instruction from the user\n- **If you encounter files/changes from another agent**, leave them alone — do not modify, revert, or clean them up\n- **Commit only your changes** — do not stage unrelated modifications with `git add -A` or `git add .`; use specific file paths\n- **If your worktree has unexpected state**, report it via task notes or `loom complete` rather than cleaning it up\n- **Do not switch branches** — you are confined to your assigned worktree branch\n\n\n## User's Initial Request\n\nREVIEW CONTRACT\ntask=MARATHON-6\nattempt=1\nbase=f4cf48192856189c3c1d1231aced023485e76550\ncandidate=99237bd3e5b46e7ea5fffde7a55afcce47438b83\n\nDESIGN:\n# MARATHON-6 — Workspace members, roles, ownership transfer\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task completes workspace tenancy beyond create/list/detail (MARATHON-5): authenticated **members** can list workspace membership; **admins/owners** can PATCH `name` / `join_mode`; **admins/owners** can change other members’ roles under a strict hierarchy; and the **owner** alone can transfer ownership to an existing **admin** (previous owner becomes admin). It locks `MemberObj`, the four REST seams SPA settings (MARATHON-18) and channel/invitation authz (MARATHON-7/12) depend on, and keeps `workspaces.owner_id` synchronized with `workspace_members.role='owner'`.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Persistence | Existing migration **v2** tables only — **no new migration** |\n| Route layout | Extend `server/workspaces/routes.py` under `/api/workspaces` |\n| Auth | Reuse `get_current_user`; all endpoints require Bearer |\n| Workspace resolution | Resolve by `slug`; unknown slug **or** non-member → **404** `not_found` (same as MARATHON-5; do not leak invite-only existence) |\n| Privilege failures | When caller **is** a member but lacks permission → **403** `forbidden` (first use of the code reserved by MARATHON-5) |\n| Ownership SoT | Dual write: `workspaces.owner_id` **and** exactly one `workspace_members.role='owner'`; transfer updates both in one transaction |\n| Role changes | `PATCH .../members/{user_id}` never creates owners; only `POST .../transfer_ownership` promotes to owner |\n| Member list enrichment | Join `users` for `username` / `display_name` (SPA settings without N+1 `GET /api/users/{id}`) |\n| Events / Redis | No pub/sub in this task (MARATHON-13/14); no Redis SoT |\n\n### Why\n\n- Schema already has `workspace_members.role` CHECK and `join_mode`; inventing a third ownership table would diverge from MARATHON-5.\n- Separating transfer from role PATCH prevents “set role to owner” shortcuts and matches the task’s 400/403 matrix.\n- Flat `MemberObj` with denormalized username/display_name matches MARATHON-5’s preference for flat workspace JSON while giving MARATHON-18 enough to render role rows.\n- 404-for-non-members preserves the privacy rule already shipped on workspace detail.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|------------|------------------|\n| Nested full `UserObj` on every member | Heavier than needed; status/avatar can be fetched via MARATHON-4 when UI wants them |\n| Allow `role: \"owner\"` on PATCH | Task mandates **400**; ownership must go through transfer |\n| Soft-fail admin→admin PATCH as no-op 200 | Task mandates **403** |\n| New migration for `updated_at` on membership | Unused by contracts; keep v2 as-is |\n| Transfer to any member (auto-promote) | Task: target **must already be admin** else **400** |\n| Distinct 404 vs 403 for non-members on privileged routes | Would leak membership; keep 404 for non-members |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nTests (and future join/invite flows) must **seed** non-owner members via SQL or later APIs until MARATHON-7/12 land. We accept that friction rather than inventing a provisional “add member” route here.\n\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\n\nFrom **MARATHON-2**: `/api/...` JSON; shared SQLite WAL; Redis not SoT.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-3**: UUID4 string ids; UTC Z timestamps in DB; `ApiError` + `{error:{code,message}}`; ignore unknown JSON body fields; `400` `validation_error`; `401` `unauthorized`; `409` `conflict` only for uniqueness (not used by these endpoints unless CHECK fails unexpectedly).\n\nFrom **MARATHON-4**: `UserObj` fields `username` / `display_name` semantics; PATCH uses `exclude_unset` (omit = leave unchanged).\n\nFrom **MARATHON-5**: `WorkspaceObj` exact keys; `validate_name` / slug rules; membership gate → 404; `join_mode` ∈ {`open`,`invite_only`}; roles ∈ {`owner`,`admin`,`member`,`guest`}; `forbidden` reserved for role rules.\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Shared types\n\n#### `WorkspaceObj` (unchanged from MARATHON-5)\n\n```json\n\nYou are cwd-ed into a DISPOSABLE detached checkout of the candidate commit. Review it against the design and acceptance criteria, then write CRITIC-VERDICT.txt in the current directory containing EXACTLY one first line:\nREVIEW attempt=1 commit=99237bd3e5b46e7ea5fffde7a55afcce47438b83 APPROVED — <reason>\nor\nREVIEW attempt=1 commit=99237bd3e5b46e7ea5fffde7a55afcce47438b83 CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\n\nAddress this request using the lead mode conventions above."}]},"session_id":"391b74f0-bbd4-4f98-8b5b-c1cd4e87d5c0"}
